# Every tracked file is LF in the working copy as well as in the index, whatever
# core.autocrlf is set to. With core.autocrlf=true and no setting here, a Windows
# checkout is CRLF, and a `\r` at the end of each line reaches the shell hooks and
# their awk helpers as data: `while IFS= read -r` in gate-test.sh compares a line
# of shell-keys.tsv against a `\r`-free expectation and reports a mismatch between
# two strings that print the same.
* text=auto eol=lf
